#### 8. Exception Handling in Tests — `addNullSkuManualCatch` (line 92)

```java
try {
    catalog.add(null, 1);
    fail("should have thrown");
} catch (Exception ex) {
    assertNotNull(ex.getMessage());
}
```

Manual `try/catch` obscures intent. If someone removes the `fail()` call, a non-throwing `add` silently passes. The catch also swallows the wrong exception type.

**Refactor → use `assertThrows` (as `addThrowsOnNegativeCount` already demonstrates):**

```java
@Test
void addThrowsOnNullSku() {
    IllegalArgumentException ex = assertThrows(
        IllegalArgumentException.class,
        () -> catalog.add(null, 1));
    assertTrue(ex.getMessage().contains("sku is required"));
}
```

